1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,850
Every body has its own normal.

2
00:00:01,950 --> 00:00:04,150
On Earth, ASTRA learns yours.

3
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:07,250
16 measures a day, for 14 days.

4
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:10,590
Then you leave Earth, and your body changes.

5
00:00:11,140 --> 00:00:13,040
Orbit mode moves your normal with you.

6
00:00:14,280 --> 00:00:15,530
Day 12. Something shifts.

7
00:00:16,130 --> 00:00:19,580
A guided check, and possible causes, with the evidence.

8
00:00:21,030 --> 00:00:24,290
On the way to Mars, help from Earth is 44 minutes away.

9
00:00:24,370 --> 00:00:28,324
AstroKinetics watches through one cabin camera and a smartwatch:

10
00:00:28,324 --> 00:00:31,099
pulse, posture and tremor — fully offline.

11
00:00:31,179 --> 00:00:34,991
It compares each astronaut with their own pre-flight baseline,

12
00:00:34,991 --> 00:00:40,275
and tells cabin CO₂, muscle strain and radiation apart — using real NASA crew data.

13
00:00:40,355 --> 00:00:45,301
Then it gives one clear action: a countermeasure, therapy audio and a wrist cue.

14
00:00:45,381 --> 00:00:47,621
From Mars to rural clinics on Earth.

15
00:00:47,971 --> 00:00:50,241
ASTRA. Know your normal.

